# Build output
notes_app
notes-app
/out/
/dist/

# Go test artifacts.
#
# These are anchored to this directory on purpose. An unanchored `coverage.*`
# also matches vendored *source*: it silently swallowed
# vendor/golang.org/x/text/language/coverage.go, and because that file defines
# language.NewCoverage, the committed vendor tree did not compile. `go build
# ./...` failed on any fresh clone with "undefined: language.NewCoverage" while
# passing on the machine that happened to still have the file lying around
# untracked. `task clean` only ever removes these two at the module root.
/*.out
/coverage.html
/coverage.txt

# Local secrets. .env.example is the tracked template and stays visible.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
